{"title": "Sectional Mock #5 (Mixed)", "duration_min": 30.0, "questions": [{"q_en": "<p>A contractor takes a contract to construct the road in 32 days and employed some no. of workers. 8 workers were absent from beginning, the rest workers completed the work in 36 days. Find the initial no. of workers?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2336;&#2375;&#2325;&#2375;&#2342;&#2366;&#2352; 32 &#2342;&#2367;&#2344;&#2379;&#2306; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2360;&#2337;&#2364;&#2325; &#2348;&#2344;&#2366;&#2344;&#2375; &#2325;&#2375; &#2354;&#2367;&#2319; &#2319;&#2325; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2348;&#2306;&#2343; &#2354;&#2375;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376; &#2324;&#2352; &#2325;&#2369;&#2331; &#2325;&#2352;&#2381;&#2350;&#2330;&#2366;&#2352;&#2367;&#2351;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2379; &#2325;&#2366;&#2350; &#2346;&#2352; &#2352;&#2326;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;| 8 &#2325;&#2352;&#2381;&#2350;&#2330;&#2366;&#2352;&#2368; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2352;&#2350;&#2381;&#2349; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2309;&#2357;&#2325;&#2366;&#2358; &#2346;&#2352; &#2341;&#2375;, &#2358;&#2375;&#2359; &#2325;&#2352;&#2381;&#2350;&#2330;&#2366;&#2352;&#2367;&#2351;&#2379;&#2306; &#2344;&#2375; &#2348;&#2330;&#2375; &#2361;&#2369;&#2319; &#2325;&#2366;&#2350; &#2325;&#2379; 36 &#2342;&#2367;&#2344;&#2379;&#2306; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2346;&#2370;&#2352;&#2366; &#2325;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366;| &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2352;&#2350;&#2381;&#2349; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2325;&#2352;&#2381;&#2350;&#2330;&#2366;&#2352;&#2367;&#2351;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2368; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2352;&#2375;&#2306;|</p>", "options_en": ["70", "71", "72", "75"], "options_hi": ["70", "71", "72", "75"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p>Let initial workers be 'w'</p><p>Total work completed in 32 days = w x 32</p><p>If 8 workers were absent from the beginning then left work is done by (w  -  8) workers in 36 days</p><p>Using formula, M<sub>1</sub>D<sub>1</sub> = M<sub>2</sub>D<sub>2</sub></p><p>=&gt; 32 x w = 36 x (w  -  8)</p><p>=&gt; W = 72</p><p>=&gt; Initial no. of workers = 72</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Let initial workers be 'w'</p><p>Total work completed in 32 days = w x 32</p><p>If 8 workers were absent from the beginning then left work is done by (w  -  8) workers in 36 days</p><p>Using formula, M<sub>1</sub>D<sub>1</sub> = M<sub>2</sub>D<sub>2</sub></p><p>=&gt; 32 x w = 36 x (w  -  8)</p><p>=&gt; W = 72</p><p>=&gt; Initial no. of workers = 72</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Time & Work"}, {"q_en": "<p>Simplify the following expression.</p><p><img width=181 height=48 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p25685/image056.png\"></p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2344;&#2367;&#2350;&#2381;&#2344;&#2354;&#2367;&#2326;&#2367;&#2340; &#2309;&#2349;&#2367;&#2357;&#2381;&#2351;&#2325;&#2381;&#2340;&#2367; &#2325;&#2379; &#2360;&#2352;&#2354; &#2348;&#2344;&#2366;&#2319;&#2306;.</p><p><img width=181 height=48 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p25685/image056.png\"></p>", "options_en": ["2", "230", "4", "1"], "options_hi": ["2", "230", "4", "1"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p><img width=181 height=48 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p25685/image057.png\"></p><p><img width=324 height=40 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p25685/image058.png\"></p><p><img width=123 height=37 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p25685/image059.png\"></p><p><img width=25 height=16 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p25685/image060.png\"></p>", "solution_hi": "<p><img width=181 height=48 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p25685/image057.png\"></p><p><img width=324 height=40 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p25685/image058.png\"></p><p><img width=123 height=37 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p25685/image059.png\"></p><p><img width=25 height=16 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p25685/image060.png\"></p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Simplification"}, {"q_en": "<p>What is the value of 1/0.9+1/0.09+1/0.009+&#8943; up to 6 terms?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>1/0.9+1/0.09+1/0.009+&#8943; &#2325;&#2375; 6 &#2346;&#2342;&#2379;&#2306; &#2340;&#2325; &#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?</p>", "options_en": ["1111110/9", "555555", "999999", "555555/9"], "options_hi": ["1111110/9", "555555", "999999", "555555/9"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p>Given series is in the form of G.P.:</p><p>Then, first term = a = (1/0.9)</p><p>Common ratio = r = (1/0.09)/(1/0.9) = 10</p><p>Total terms = n = 6</p><p>Therefore, sum = a(r<sup>n</sup>  -  1)/(r  -  1)</p><p>= (1/0.9)(10<sup>6</sup>  -  1)/(10  -  1)</p><p><b>= 1111110/9</b></p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Given series is in the form of G.P.:</p><p>Then, first term = a = (1/0.9)</p><p>Common ratio = r = (1/0.09)/(1/0.9) = 10</p><p>Total terms = n = 6</p><p>Therefore, sum = a(r<sup>n</sup>  -  1)/(r  -  1)</p><p>= (1/0.9)(10<sup>6</sup>  -  1)/(10  -  1)</p><p><b>= 1111110/9</b></p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Number System"}, {"q_en": "<p>If sec <i>a</i> = X and cosec <i>a</i> = Y, then X<sup>2 </sup>+ Y<sup>2</sup> = ?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; sec <i>a</i> = X &#2324;&#2352; cosec <i>a</i> = Y &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; X<sup>2 </sup>+ Y<sup>2</sup>=?</p>", "options_en": ["XY", "X<sup>2</sup>Y<sup>2</sup> - XY", "X<sup>2</sup>Y<sup>2</sup> + XY", "X<sup>2</sup>Y<sup>2</sup>"], "options_hi": ["XY", "X<sup>2</sup>Y<sup>2</sup>-XY", "X<sup>2</sup>Y<sup>2</sup>+XY", "X<sup>2</sup>Y<sup>2</sup>"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p>Given: sec<i>a</i> = X and cosec<i>a</i> = Y</p><p>X<sup>2</sup> + Y<sup>2</sup> = sec<sup>2</sup>a + cosec<sup>2</sup>a</p><p>= {1}/{cos<sup>2</sup>a} + {1}/{sin<sup>2</sup>a}</p><p>= {sin<sup>2</sup>a + cos<sup>2</sup>a}/{sin<sup>2</sup>a&#215;cos<sup>2</sup>a}</p><p>We know that cos<sup>2</sup>a + sin<sup>2</sup>a = 1</p><p>So, X<sup>2</sup> + Y<sup>2</sup> = <inlineformula>{1}/{sin<sup>2</sup>a&#215;cos<sup>2</sup>a}</inlineformula> = cosec<sup>2</sup>a&#215;sec<sup>2</sup>a = X<sup>2</sup>Y<sup>2</sup></p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Given: sec<i>a</i> = X and cosec<i>a</i> = Y</p><p>X<sup>2</sup> + Y<sup>2</sup> = sec<sup>2</sup>a + cosec<sup>2</sup>a</p><p>= {1}/{cos<sup>2</sup>a} + {1}/{sin<sup>2</sup>a}</p><p>= {sin<sup>2</sup>a + cos<sup>2</sup>a}/{sin<sup>2</sup>a&#215;cos<sup>2</sup>a}</p><p>We know that cos<sup>2</sup>a + sin<sup>2</sup>a = 1</p><p>So, X<sup>2</sup> + Y<sup>2</sup> = <inlineformula>{1}/{sin<sup>2</sup>a&#215;cos<sup>2</sup>a}</inlineformula> = cosec<sup>2</sup>a&#215;sec<sup>2</sup>a = X<sup>2</sup>Y<sup>2</sup></p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Trigonometry"}, {"q_en": "<p>If 256a<sup>4</sup> + 64a<sup>2</sup>b<sup>2</sup> + 16b<sup>4</sup> = 864 and 16a<sup>2</sup> + 4b<sup>2</sup>  -  8ab = 36, then what is the value of 4ab?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; 256a<sup>4</sup> + 64a<sup>2</sup>b<sup>2</sup> + 16b<sup>4</sup> = 864 &#2340;&#2341;&#2366; 16a<sup>2</sup> + 4b<sup>2</sup> - 8ab = 36, &#2340;&#2379; 4ab &#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2325;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?</p>", "options_en": ["12", "-3", "-12", "3"], "options_hi": ["12", "-3", "-12", "3"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>16a<sup>2</sup> + 4b<sup>2</sup>  -  8ab = 36 .... (i)</p><p>256a<sup>4</sup> + 64a<sup>2</sup>b<sup>2</sup> + 16b<sup>2</sup> = 864</p><p>(16a<sup>2</sup>)<sup>2</sup> + 16a<sup>2</sup> * 4b<sup>2</sup> + (4b<sup>2</sup>)<sup>2</sup> = 864 </p><p>(16a<sup>2</sup> + 8ab + 4b<sup>2</sup>) (16a<sup>2</sup>  -  8ab + 4b<sup>2</sup>) = 864 </p><p>(16a<sup>2</sup> + 8ab + 4b<sup>2</sup>) * 36 = 864 </p><p>16a<sup>2</sup> + 8ab + 4b<sup>2</sup> = 24 .... (ii)</p><p>Subtract (i) from (ii)</p><p>16ab = -12</p><p>4ab = -12/4 = -3 </p>", "solution_hi": "<p>16a<sup>2</sup> + 4b<sup>2</sup>  -  8ab = 36 .... (i)</p><p>256a<sup>4</sup> + 64a<sup>2</sup>b<sup>2</sup> + 16b<sup>2</sup> = 864</p><p>(16a<sup>2</sup>)<sup>2</sup> + 16a<sup>2</sup> * 4b<sup>2</sup> + (4b<sup>2</sup>)<sup>2</sup> = 864 </p><p>(16a<sup>2</sup> + 8ab + 4b<sup>2</sup>) (16a<sup>2</sup>  -  8ab + 4b<sup>2</sup>) = 864 </p><p>(16a<sup>2</sup> + 8ab + 4b<sup>2</sup>) * 36 = 864 </p><p>16a<sup>2</sup> + 8ab + 4b<sup>2</sup> = 24 .... (ii)</p><p>Subtract (i) from (ii)</p><p>16ab = -12</p><p>4ab = -12/4 = -3 </p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Algebra"}, {"q_en": "<p>A 12 litre solution of acid and water contains 30% acid. How much water (in litres) must be added to get a solution having 20% acid?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2309;&#2350;&#2381;&#2354; &#2324;&#2352; &#2346;&#2366;&#2344;&#2368; &#2325;&#2375; 12 &#2354;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352; &#2328;&#2379;&#2354; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; 30% &#2309;&#2350;&#2381;&#2354; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; 20% &#2309;&#2350;&#2381;&#2354; &#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2366; &#2328;&#2379;&#2354; &#2348;&#2344;&#2366;&#2344;&#2375; &#2325;&#2375; &#2354;&#2367;&#2319; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2366; &#2346;&#2366;&#2344;&#2368; (&#2354;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306;) &#2350;&#2367;&#2354;&#2366;&#2344;&#2366; &#2361;&#2379;&#2327;&#2366;?</p>", "options_en": ["6", "3", "5", "4"], "options_hi": ["6", "3", "5", "4"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p>Acid = 30%  X  12 = 3.6 L</p><p>Let water added = x L</p><p>New volume = 12 + x</p><p>[3.6/(12 + x)]  X  100 = 20</p><p>12 + x = 18</p><p>x = 6</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Acid = 30%  X  12 = 3.6 L</p><p>Let water added = x L</p><p>New volume = 12 + x</p><p>[3.6/(12 + x)]  X  100 = 20</p><p>12 + x = 18</p><p>x = 6</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Mixture & Alligation"}, {"q_en": "<p>A cat climbs to the top of a pole that is X meters tall, positioned 2X meters away from a tall tree. From the top of the pole, the cat looks up at an angle of 45&deg; to see the top of the tree. What is the height of the tree?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2348;&#2367;&#2354;&#2381;&#2354;&#2368; &#2319;&#2325; &#2326;&#2306;&#2349;&#2375; &#2325;&#2375; &#2358;&#2368;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359; &#2346;&#2352; &#2330;&#2338;&#2364;&#2340;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376; &#2332;&#2379; X &#2350;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352; &#2314;&#2306;&#2330;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2332;&#2379; &#2319;&#2325; &#2314;&#2306;&#2330;&#2375; &#2346;&#2375;&#2337;&#2364; &#2360;&#2375; 2X &#2350;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352; &#2325;&#2368; &#2342;&#2370;&#2352;&#2368; &#2346;&#2352; &#2360;&#2381;&#2341;&#2367;&#2340; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2326;&#2306;&#2349;&#2375; &#2325;&#2375; &#2358;&#2368;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359; &#2360;&#2375;, &#2348;&#2367;&#2354;&#2381;&#2354;&#2368; &#2346;&#2375;&#2337;&#2364; &#2325;&#2375; &#2358;&#2368;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359; &#2325;&#2379; &#2342;&#2375;&#2326;&#2344;&#2375; &#2325;&#2375; &#2354;&#2367;&#2319; 45&deg; &#2325;&#2375; &#2325;&#2379;&#2339; &#2346;&#2352; &#2342;&#2375;&#2326;&#2340;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2346;&#2375;&#2337;&#2364; &#2325;&#2368; &#2314;&#2306;&#2330;&#2366;&#2312; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;?</p>", "options_en": ["X/3", "3X", "3X/2", "X/3"], "options_hi": ["X/3", "3X", "3X/2", "X/3"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p><img width=219 height=319 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p27673/image003.png\"></p><p>In triangle CAB,</p><p>tan45&deg; = CB/BA</p><p>1 = CB/BA</p><p>CB = BA = 2X m</p><p>Height of building CD = CB + BD = 2X + X = 3x.</p>", "solution_hi": "<p><img width=219 height=319 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p27673/image003.png\"></p><p>In triangle CAB,</p><p>tan45&deg; = CB/BA</p><p>1 = CB/BA</p><p>CB = BA = 2X m</p><p>Height of building CD = CB + BD = 2X + X = 3x.</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Height & Distance"}, {"q_en": "<p>In a team of some members, a new member weighing 81 kg joins, then the average weight of the team increased by 1 kg. If the weight of the new member had been 39 kg, then the average weight of the members would have decreased by 1 kg. The actual average weight of the team is - </p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2325;&#2369;&#2331; &#2360;&#2342;&#2360;&#2381;&#2351;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2368; &#2319;&#2325; &#2335;&#2368;&#2350; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; 81 &#2325;&#2367;&#2354;&#2379;&#2327;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2350; &#2357;&#2332;&#2344; &#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2366; &#2319;&#2325; &#2344;&#2351;&#2366; &#2360;&#2342;&#2360;&#2381;&#2351; &#2358;&#2366;&#2350;&#2367;&#2354; &#2361;&#2379;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2335;&#2368;&#2350; &#2325;&#2366; &#2324;&#2360;&#2340; &#2357;&#2332;&#2344; 1 &#2325;&#2367;&#2354;&#2379;&#2327;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2350; &#2348;&#2338;&#2364; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2344;&#2319; &#2360;&#2342;&#2360;&#2381;&#2351; &#2325;&#2366; &#2357;&#2332;&#2344; 39 &#2325;&#2367;&#2354;&#2379;&#2327;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2350; &#2361;&#2379;&#2340;&#2366;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2360;&#2342;&#2360;&#2381;&#2351;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2366; &#2324;&#2360;&#2340; &#2357;&#2332;&#2344; 1 &#2325;&#2367;&#2354;&#2379;&#2327;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2350; &#2325;&#2350; &#2361;&#2379; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366;&#2404; &#2335;&#2368;&#2350; &#2325;&#2366; &#2357;&#2366;&#2360;&#2381;&#2340;&#2357;&#2367;&#2325; &#2324;&#2360;&#2340; &#2357;&#2332;&#2344; &#2361;&#2376; - </p>", "options_en": ["60 kg", "70 kg", "64 kg", "72 kg"], "options_hi": ["60 &#2325;&#2367;&#2354;&#2379;", "70 &#2325;&#2367;&#2354;&#2379;", "64 &#2325;&#2367;&#2354;&#2379;", "72 &#2325;&#2367;&#2354;&#2379;"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p>Let total number of members in the team = n</p><p>Actual average weight of the team = w kg</p><p>Now,</p><p>nw + 81 = (n + 1)(w + 1) ------(1)</p><p>nw + 39 = (n + 1)(w  -  1) ------(2)</p><p>From (1) and (2)  -</p><p>(n + 1)*2 = 42</p><p>n = 20</p><p>20w + 81 = 21w + 21</p><p>w = 60 kg</p><p></p><p><b> Express Method </b></p><p>81 kg joins the average increases by 1.</p><p>39 kg joins the average decreases by 1.</p><p>Actual average = Average of 81 and 39 = 60 kg</p><p></p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Let total number of members in the team = n</p><p>Actual average weight of the team = w kg</p><p>Now,</p><p>nw + 81 = (n + 1)(w + 1) ------(1)</p><p>nw + 39 = (n + 1)(w  -  1) ------(2)</p><p>From (1) and (2)  -</p><p>(n + 1)*2 = 42</p><p>n = 20</p><p>20w + 81 = 21w + 21</p><p>w = 60 kg</p><p></p><p><b> Express Method </b></p><p>81 kg joins the average increases by 1.</p><p>39 kg joins the average decreases by 1.</p><p>Actual average = Average of 81 and 39 = 60 kg</p><p></p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Average"}, {"q_en": "<p>Find the median of the following data:</p><p>24, 58, 39, 50, 32, 7, 10, 36, 25, 42, 21, 18</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2344;&#2367;&#2350;&#2381;&#2344;&#2354;&#2367;&#2326;&#2367;&#2340; &#2310;&#2305;&#2325;&#2337;&#2364;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2366;&#2343;&#2381;&#2351;&#2367;&#2325;&#2366; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;:</p><p>24, 58, 39, 50, 32, 7, 10, 36, 25, 42, 21, 18</p>", "options_en": ["27", "27.5", "28", "28.5"], "options_hi": ["27", "27.5", "28", "28.5"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p>Data: 24, 58, 39, 50, 32, 7, 10, 36, 25, 42, 21, 18</p><p>Data in ascending order: 7, 10, 18, 21, 24, 25, 32, 36, 39, 42, 50, 58</p><p>Median = [(12/2) + (12/2 + 1)]th terms/2 = (25 + 32)/2 = 28.5</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Data: 24, 58, 39, 50, 32, 7, 10, 36, 25, 42, 21, 18</p><p>Data in ascending order: 7, 10, 18, 21, 24, 25, 32, 36, 39, 42, 50, 58</p><p>Median = [(12/2) + (12/2 + 1)]th terms/2 = (25 + 32)/2 = 28.5</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Statistics"}, {"q_en": "<p>Find the factors of the expression 3x<sup>2</sup>  -  16x + 5.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2357;&#2381;&#2351;&#2306;&#2332;&#2325; 3x<sup>2</sup> - 16x + 5 &#2325;&#2375; &#2327;&#2369;&#2339;&#2344;&#2326;&#2306;&#2337; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2352;&#2375;&#2306;</p>", "options_en": ["(x  -  5) and (3x  -  1)", "(x + 5) and (3x  -  1)", "(x + 5) and (3x + 1)", "(x  -  5) and (3x + 1)"], "options_hi": ["(x - 5) &#2324;&#2352; (3x - 1)", "(x + 5) &#2324;&#2352; (3x - 1)", "(x + 5) &#2324;&#2352; (3x + 1)", "(x - 5) &#2324;&#2352; (3x + 1)"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p>3x<sup>2</sup>  -  16x + 5</p><p>= 3x<sup>2</sup>  -  15x  -  x + 5</p><p>= 3x (x  -  5)  -  1 (x  -  5)</p><p>= (x  -  5) (3x  -  1)</p><p>Hence, required factors are (x  -  5) and (3x  -  1).</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>3x<sup>2</sup>  -  16x + 5</p><p>= 3x<sup>2</sup>  -  15x  -  x + 5</p><p>= 3x (x  -  5)  -  1 (x  -  5)</p><p>= (x  -  5) (3x  -  1)</p><p>Hence, required factors are (x  -  5) and (3x  -  1).</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "HCF & LCM"}, {"q_en": "<p>Which of the following expression (s) is/are true?</p><p>I. &radic;5+&radic;5 &gt; &radic;2+2&radic;2</p><p>II. &radic;4+&radic;7 &gt; &radic;2+&radic;8</p><p>III. &radic;6+&radic;8 &lt; &radic;4+&radic;12</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2344;&#2367;&#2350;&#2381;&#2344;&#2354;&#2367;&#2326;&#2367;&#2340; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2360;&#2375; &#2325;&#2380;&#2344;-&#2360;&#2366;/&#2360;&#2375; &#2357;&#2381;&#2351;&#2306;&#2332;&#2325; &#2360;&#2340;&#2381;&#2351; &#2361;&#2376;/&#2361;&#2376;&#2306;?</p><p>I. &radic;5+&radic;5 &gt; &radic;2+2&radic;2</p><p>II. &radic;4+&radic;7 &gt; &radic;2+&radic;8</p><p>III. &radic;6+&radic;8 &lt; &radic;4+&radic;12</p>", "options_en": ["Only I", "Only II", "Only III", "All expressions are true"], "options_hi": ["&#2325;&#2375;&#2357;&#2354; I", "&#2325;&#2375;&#2357;&#2354; II", "&#2325;&#2375;&#2357;&#2354; III", "&#2360;&#2349;&#2368; &#2357;&#2381;&#2351;&#2306;&#2332;&#2325; &#2360;&#2340;&#2381;&#2351; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p>I. &radic;5+&radic;5 &gt; &radic;2+2&radic;2</p><p>Squaring both side we get,</p><p>10+2&radic;25 &gt; 10+2&radic;16</p><p>2&radic;25 &gt; 2&radic;16</p><p>10 &gt; 8</p><p>True</p><p>II. &radic;4+&radic;7 &gt; &radic;2+&radic;8</p><p>Squaring both side we get,</p><p>11+2&radic;28 &gt; 10+2&radic;16</p><p>True</p><p>III. &radic;6+&radic;8 &lt; &radic;4+&radic;12</p><p>Squaring both side we get,</p><p>14+2&radic;48 &lt; 16+2&radic;48</p><p>True</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>I. &radic;5+&radic;5 &gt; &radic;2+2&radic;2</p><p>Squaring both side we get,</p><p>10+2&radic;25 &gt; 10+2&radic;16</p><p>2&radic;25 &gt; 2&radic;16</p><p>10 &gt; 8</p><p>True</p><p>II. &radic;4+&radic;7 &gt; &radic;2+&radic;8</p><p>Squaring both side we get,</p><p>11+2&radic;28 &gt; 10+2&radic;16</p><p>True</p><p>III. &radic;6+&radic;8 &lt; &radic;4+&radic;12</p><p>Squaring both side we get,</p><p>14+2&radic;48 &lt; 16+2&radic;48</p><p>True</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Mixed Practice"}, {"q_en": "<p>Which of the following line passes through the midpoint of line segment joining points (3,4) and (-2,7)?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2344;&#2367;&#2350;&#2381;&#2344; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2360;&#2375; &#2325;&#2380;&#2344; &#2360;&#2368; &#2352;&#2375;&#2326;&#2366; &#2332;&#2369;&#2396;&#2366;&#2357; &#2348;&#2367;&#2344;&#2381;&#2342;&#2369;&#2323;&#2306; (3,4) &#2324;&#2352; (-2,7) &#2325;&#2375; &#2352;&#2375;&#2326;&#2366; &#2326;&#2306;&#2337; &#2325;&#2375; &#2350;&#2343;&#2381;&#2351; &#2348;&#2367;&#2306;&#2342;&#2369; &#2360;&#2375; &#2361;&#2379;&#2325;&#2352; &#2327;&#2369;&#2332;&#2352;&#2340;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;?</p>", "options_en": ["y = 10 - 9x", "y = 3 + 5x", "y = 5 -2x", "Both (1) and (2)"], "options_hi": ["y = 10 - 9x", "y = 3 + 5x", "y = 5 -2x", "(1) &#2324;&#2352; (2) &#2342;&#2379;&#2344;&#2379;&#2306;"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p>According to the mid-point formula (x, y) coordinates of mid- point</p><p>x = (3 +(-2)) /2 = 0.5</p><p>y = (4 + 7)/2 = 5.5</p><p>So, line passing through mid-point must satisfy its equation for given set of values.</p><p>According to option (1)</p><p>5.5 = 10  -  (9 x 0.5) = 5.5</p><p>LHS = RHS hence line passes through mid-point.</p><p>According to option (2)</p><p>5.5 = 3 + (5 x 0.5) = 5.5</p><p>LHS = RHS hence line passes through mid-point.</p><p>According to option (3)</p><p>5.5 = 5  -  (2 x 0.5) = 4</p><p>LHS is not equal to RHS hence line does not pass through mid-point.</p><p>Hence correct answer is option (4).</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>According to the mid-point formula (x, y) coordinates of mid- point</p><p>x = (3 +(-2)) /2 = 0.5</p><p>y = (4 + 7)/2 = 5.5</p><p>So, line passing through mid-point must satisfy its equation for given set of values.</p><p>According to option (1)</p><p>5.5 = 10  -  (9 x 0.5) = 5.5</p><p>LHS = RHS hence line passes through mid-point.</p><p>According to option (2)</p><p>5.5 = 3 + (5 x 0.5) = 5.5</p><p>LHS = RHS hence line passes through mid-point.</p><p>According to option (3)</p><p>5.5 = 5  -  (2 x 0.5) = 4</p><p>LHS is not equal to RHS hence line does not pass through mid-point.</p><p>Hence correct answer is option (4).</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Mensuration (2D)"}, {"q_en": "<p>The probability of encoding a problem by A is 9/14 and the probability of solving a problem by B and C are 8/11, and 7/9 respectively. The probability that the problem will be solved is:</p>", "q_hi": "<p>A &#2342;&#2381;&#2357;&#2366;&#2352;&#2366; &#2325;&#2367;&#2360;&#2368; &#2360;&#2350;&#2360;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2325;&#2379; &#2319;&#2344;&#2325;&#2379;&#2337; &#2325;&#2352;&#2344;&#2375; &#2325;&#2368; &#2360;&#2306;&#2349;&#2366;&#2357;&#2344;&#2366; 9/14 &#2361;&#2376; &#2324;&#2352; B &#2340;&#2341;&#2366; C &#2342;&#2381;&#2357;&#2366;&#2352;&#2366; &#2325;&#2367;&#2360;&#2368; &#2360;&#2350;&#2360;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2325;&#2379; &#2361;&#2354; &#2325;&#2352;&#2344;&#2375; &#2325;&#2368; &#2360;&#2306;&#2349;&#2366;&#2357;&#2344;&#2366; &#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2350;&#2358;&#2307; 8/11 &#2340;&#2341;&#2366; 7/9 &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2360;&#2350;&#2360;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2325;&#2375; &#2361;&#2354; &#2361;&#2379;&#2344;&#2375; &#2325;&#2368; &#2360;&#2306;&#2349;&#2366;&#2357;&#2344;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;:</p>", "options_en": ["3/77", "4/11", "20/99", "74/77"], "options_hi": ["3/77", "4/11", "20/99", "74/77"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p>P(B') = 1  -  8/11 = 3/11 </p><p>P(C') = 1  -  7/9 = 2/9 </p><p>The probability of encoding = 9/14 * 3/11 * 2/9 = 3/77 </p><p>Hence, the required probability = 1  -  3/77 = 74/77</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>P(B') = 1  -  8/11 = 3/11 </p><p>P(C') = 1  -  7/9 = 2/9 </p><p>The probability of encoding = 9/14 * 3/11 * 2/9 = 3/77 </p><p>Hence, the required probability = 1  -  3/77 = 74/77</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Probability"}, {"q_en": "<p>The following pie chart shows the percentage of students applied for a scholarship test from four different states  -  state A, state B, state C and state D.</p><p>Total number of students applied for the test = 4000</p><p><img width=351 height=320 id=\"Chart 1\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p15926/image001.png\"></p><p>The following bar graph shows the ratio between the number of boys and number of girls applied for the test from different states.</p><p><img width=576 height=336 id=\"Chart 2\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/other/er221026ssclt9-002.png\"></p><p></p><p>Find the difference between the number of boys from state B and state C together and the number of girls from state B and state D together applied for the test.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2344;&#2367;&#2350;&#2381;&#2344;&#2354;&#2367;&#2326;&#2367;&#2340; &#2357;&#2371;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340;&#2368;&#2351; &#2310;&#2352;&#2375;&#2326; &#2330;&#2366;&#2352; &#2309;&#2354;&#2327;-&#2309;&#2354;&#2327; &#2352;&#2366;&#2332;&#2381;&#2351;&#2379;&#2306; - &#2352;&#2366;&#2332;&#2381;&#2351; A, &#2352;&#2366;&#2332;&#2381;&#2351; B, &#2352;&#2366;&#2332;&#2381;&#2351; C &#2324;&#2352; &#2352;&#2366;&#2332;&#2381;&#2351; D &#2360;&#2375; &#2331;&#2366;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2357;&#2371;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340;&#2367; &#2346;&#2352;&#2368;&#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2366; &#2325;&#2375; &#2354;&#2367;&#2319; &#2310;&#2357;&#2375;&#2342;&#2344; &#2325;&#2352;&#2344;&#2375; &#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2375; &#2357;&#2367;&#2342;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2352;&#2381;&#2341;&#2367;&#2351;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2375; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367;&#2358;&#2340; &#2325;&#2379; &#2342;&#2352;&#2381;&#2358;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404;</p><p>&#2346;&#2352;&#2368;&#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2366; &#2325;&#2375; &#2354;&#2367;&#2319; &#2310;&#2357;&#2375;&#2342;&#2344; &#2325;&#2352;&#2344;&#2375; &#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2375; &#2357;&#2367;&#2342;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2352;&#2381;&#2341;&#2367;&#2351;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2368; &#2325;&#2369;&#2354; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; = 4000</p><p><img width=\"351\" height=\"320\" id=\"Chart 1\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p15926/image001.png\"></p><p>&#2344;&#2367;&#2350;&#2381;&#2344;&#2354;&#2367;&#2326;&#2367;&#2340; &#2342;&#2306;&#2337; &#2310;&#2352;&#2375;&#2326; &#2309;&#2354;&#2327;-&#2309;&#2354;&#2327; &#2352;&#2366;&#2332;&#2381;&#2351;&#2379;&#2306; &#2360;&#2375; &#2346;&#2352;&#2368;&#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2366; &#2325;&#2375; &#2354;&#2367;&#2319; &#2310;&#2357;&#2375;&#2342;&#2344; &#2325;&#2352;&#2344;&#2375; &#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2375; &#2354;&#2337;&#2364;&#2325;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2368; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2324;&#2352; &#2354;&#2337;&#2364;&#2325;&#2367;&#2351;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2368; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2325;&#2375; &#2348;&#2368;&#2330; &#2325;&#2375; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2379; &#2342;&#2352;&#2381;&#2358;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404;</p><p><img width=\"576\" height=\"336\" id=\"Chart 2\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/other/er221026ssclt9-002.png\"></p><p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2360;&#2366;&#2341; &#2352;&#2366;&#2332;&#2381;&#2351; B &#2324;&#2352; &#2352;&#2366;&#2332;&#2381;&#2351; C &#2360;&#2375; &#2346;&#2352;&#2368;&#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2366; &#2325;&#2375; &#2354;&#2367;&#2319; &#2310;&#2357;&#2375;&#2342;&#2344; &#2325;&#2352;&#2344;&#2375; &#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2375; &#2354;&#2337;&#2364;&#2325;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2368; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2340;&#2341;&#2366; &#2319;&#2325; &#2360;&#2366;&#2341; &#2352;&#2366;&#2332;&#2381;&#2351; B &#2324;&#2352; &#2352;&#2366;&#2332;&#2381;&#2351; D &#2360;&#2375; &#2346;&#2352;&#2368;&#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2366; &#2325;&#2375; &#2354;&#2367;&#2319; &#2310;&#2357;&#2375;&#2342;&#2344; &#2325;&#2352;&#2344;&#2375; &#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2368; &#2354;&#2337;&#2364;&#2325;&#2367;&#2351;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2368; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2325;&#2375; &#2348;&#2368;&#2330; &#2325;&#2366; &#2309;&#2306;&#2340;&#2352; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["136", "124", "144", "132"], "options_hi": ["136", "124", "144", "132"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p>Number of student applied from state B = 4000 * 19/100 = 760</p><p>Number of boys applied from state B = 760 * 11/19 = 440</p><p>Number of girls applied from state B = 760  -  440 = 320</p><p>Number of student applied from state C = 4000 * 31/100 = 1240</p><p>Number of boys applied from state C = 1240 * 2/5 = 248 * 2 = 496</p><p>Number of student applied from state D = 4000 * 27/100 = 1080</p><p>Number of girls applied from state D = 1080 * 4/9 = 480</p><p>Required difference = (440 + 496)  -  (320 + 480) = 936  -  800 = 136.</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Number of student applied from state B = 4000 * 19/100 = 760</p><p>Number of boys applied from state B = 760 * 11/19 = 440</p><p>Number of girls applied from state B = 760  -  440 = 320</p><p>Number of student applied from state C = 4000 * 31/100 = 1240</p><p>Number of boys applied from state C = 1240 * 2/5 = 248 * 2 = 496</p><p>Number of student applied from state D = 4000 * 27/100 = 1080</p><p>Number of girls applied from state D = 1080 * 4/9 = 480</p><p>Required difference = (440 + 496)  -  (320 + 480) = 936  -  800 = 136.</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Percentage"}, {"q_en": "<p style=\"user-select: auto;\"><span style=\"user-select: auto;\">&nbsp;The radius of a sphere is 6 cm. It is melted and&nbsp;", "q_hi": "<p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2327;&#2379;&#2354;&#2375; &#2325;&#2368; &#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2332;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; 6 cm &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2311;&#2360;&#2375; &#2346;&#2367;&#2328;&#2354;&#2366;&#2325;&#2352; 0.2 cm &#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2332;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2366; &#2319;&#2325; &#2340;&#2366;&#2352; &#2348;&#2344;&#2366;&#2351;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2340;&#2366;&#2352; &#2325;&#2368; &#2354;&#2306;&#2348;&#2366;&#2312; &#2361;&#2376;-</p>", "options_en": ["81 m", "80 m", "75 m", "72 m"], "options_hi": ["81 m", "80 m", "75 m", "72 m"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "\"<p style=\"user-select: auto;\"><span style=\"user-select: auto;\"><img src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/stubeimg/SSCT-MML-006421.png\"/>&nbsp;&nbsp;</span></p>\"", "solution_hi": "\"<p style=\"user-select: auto;\"><span style=\"user-select: auto;\"><img src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/stubeimg/SSCT-MML-006421.png\"/>&nbsp;&nbsp;</span></p>\"", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Mensuration (3D)"}, {"q_en": "<p>Pipe A and pipe B together can fill a cistern in 28 minutes, pipe B and pipe C together can fill the same cistern in 42 minutes, and pipe A and pipe C together can fill the same cistern in 56 minutes. Find the time taken by pipe C alone to fill the cistern. </p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2360;&#2366;&#2341; &#2346;&#2366;&#2311;&#2346; A &#2324;&#2352; &#2346;&#2366;&#2311;&#2346; B &#2319;&#2325; &#2335;&#2306;&#2325;&#2368; &#2325;&#2379; 28 &#2350;&#2367;&#2344;&#2335; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2349;&#2352; &#2360;&#2325;&#2340;&#2375; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;, &#2319;&#2325; &#2360;&#2366;&#2341; &#2346;&#2366;&#2311;&#2346; B &#2324;&#2352; &#2346;&#2366;&#2311;&#2346; C &#2360;&#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2335;&#2306;&#2325;&#2368; &#2325;&#2379; 42 &#2350;&#2367;&#2344;&#2335; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2349;&#2352; &#2360;&#2325;&#2340;&#2375; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306; &#2340;&#2341;&#2366; &#2319;&#2325; &#2360;&#2366;&#2341; &#2346;&#2366;&#2311;&#2346; A &#2324;&#2352; &#2346;&#2366;&#2311;&#2346; C &#2360;&#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2335;&#2306;&#2325;&#2368; &#2325;&#2379; 56 &#2350;&#2367;&#2344;&#2335; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2349;&#2352; &#2360;&#2325;&#2340;&#2375; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;&#2404; &#2309;&#2325;&#2375;&#2354;&#2375; &#2346;&#2366;&#2311;&#2346; C &#2342;&#2381;&#2357;&#2366;&#2352;&#2366; &#2335;&#2306;&#2325;&#2368; &#2325;&#2379; &#2349;&#2352;&#2344;&#2375; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2354;&#2327;&#2344;&#2375; &#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2366; &#2360;&#2350;&#2351; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["4 hours 32 minutes", "5 hours 36 minutes", "6 hours 30 minutes", "7 hours 24minutes"], "options_hi": ["4 &#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2375; 32 &#2350;&#2367;&#2344;&#2335;", "5 &#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2375; 36 &#2350;&#2367;&#2344;&#2335;", "6 &#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2375; 30 &#2350;&#2367;&#2344;&#2335;", "7 &#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2375; 24 &#2350;&#2367;&#2344;&#2335;"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>The capacity of a cistern = L.C.M of 28, 42, and 56 = 168</p><p>Efficiency = total capacity/ time taken</p><p>Efficiency of pipe A and pipe B = 168/28 = 6</p><p>Efficiency of pipe B and pipe C = 168/42 = 4</p><p>Efficiency of pipe A and pipe C = 168/56 = 3</p><p>Efficiency of pipe A, pipe B, and pipe C = (6 + 4 + 3)/2 = 13/2</p><p>Efficiency of pipe C = 13/2  -  6 = 1/2</p><p>The required value = 168/ (1/2) = 336 minutes = 5 hours 36 minutes</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>The capacity of a cistern = L.C.M of 28, 42, and 56 = 168</p><p>Efficiency = total capacity/ time taken</p><p>Efficiency of pipe A and pipe B = 168/28 = 6</p><p>Efficiency of pipe B and pipe C = 168/42 = 4</p><p>Efficiency of pipe A and pipe C = 168/56 = 3</p><p>Efficiency of pipe A, pipe B, and pipe C = (6 + 4 + 3)/2 = 13/2</p><p>Efficiency of pipe C = 13/2  -  6 = 1/2</p><p>The required value = 168/ (1/2) = 336 minutes = 5 hours 36 minutes</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Pipes & Cisterns"}, {"q_en": "<p>A sum of Rs. 125 is lent by a child to his friend to be returned in 10 monthly installments of Rs. 13.75 each, the rate of interest is: </p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2348;&#2330;&#2381;&#2330;&#2375; &#2344;&#2375; &#2309;&#2346;&#2344;&#2375; &#2342;&#2379;&#2360;&#2381;&#2340; &#2325;&#2379; 125 &#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2351;&#2375; &#2325;&#2368; &#2352;&#2366;&#2358;&#2367; 13.75 &#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2351;&#2375; &#2325;&#2368; 10 &#2350;&#2366;&#2360;&#2367;&#2325; &#2325;&#2367;&#2360;&#2381;&#2340;&#2379;&#2306; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2357;&#2366;&#2346;&#2360; &#2325;&#2352;&#2344;&#2375; &#2325;&#2375; &#2354;&#2367;&#2319; &#2313;&#2343;&#2366;&#2352; &#2342;&#2368;, &#2348;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2332; &#2325;&#2368; &#2342;&#2352; &#2361;&#2376;: </p>", "options_en": ["12%", "18%", "16%", "20%"], "options_hi": ["12%", "18%", "16%", "20%"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p>Amount = 13.75 * Total time = 13.75 * 10 </p><p>= Rs. 137.5 </p><p>Amount  -  Principal = S.I = P * R * T/100 </p><p>137.5  -  125 = 125 * 10 * R/ (100 * 12) </p><p>12.5 = 25R/24</p><p>R = 12%</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Amount = 13.75 * Total time = 13.75 * 10 </p><p>= Rs. 137.5 </p><p>Amount  -  Principal = S.I = P * R * T/100 </p><p>137.5  -  125 = 125 * 10 * R/ (100 * 12) </p><p>12.5 = 25R/24</p><p>R = 12%</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Simple & Compound Interest"}, {"q_en": "<p>Find the value of S/2 if S = 21 + 27 + 33 + ...... till 24 terms.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; S = 21 + 27 + 33 + ...... 24 &#2346;&#2342;&#2379;&#2306; &#2340;&#2325; S/2 &#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["1080", "900", "1200", "960"], "options_hi": ["1080", "900", "1200", "960"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p>S = 21 + 27 + 33 + ..... Till 24 terms</p><p>This is an arithmetic progression with a = 21, d = 6, n = 24</p><p>We know that,</p><p>Sum (S) = (n/2) [2a + (n  -  1) x d]</p><p>S = 12 [42 + 23 x 6]</p><p>S = 12 x 180</p><p>S/2 = 6 x 180 = 1080</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>S = 21 + 27 + 33 + ..... Till 24 terms</p><p>This is an arithmetic progression with a = 21, d = 6, n = 24</p><p>We know that,</p><p>Sum (S) = (n/2) [2a + (n  -  1) x d]</p><p>S = 12 [42 + 23 x 6]</p><p>S = 12 x 180</p><p>S/2 = 6 x 180 = 1080</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Ratio & Proportion"}, {"q_en": "<p>A boat can covers 144 km in upstream in 24 hours and 168 km in downstream in 1008 minutes, then in how much time the boat can cover 54 km in upstream and 45 km in downstream?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2344;&#2366;&#2357; 24 &#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2375; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2343;&#2366;&#2352;&#2366; &#2325;&#2375; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367;&#2325;&#2370;&#2354; 144 &#2325;&#2367;&#2350;&#2368; &#2324;&#2352; &#2343;&#2366;&#2352;&#2366; &#2325;&#2375; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2325;&#2370;&#2354; 1008 &#2350;&#2367;&#2344;&#2335; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; 168 &#2325;&#2367;&#2350;&#2368; &#2325;&#2368; &#2342;&#2370;&#2352;&#2368; &#2340;&#2351; &#2325;&#2352; &#2360;&#2325;&#2340;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2344;&#2366;&#2357; &#2343;&#2366;&#2352;&#2366; &#2325;&#2375; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367;&#2325;&#2370;&#2354; 54 &#2325;&#2367;&#2350;&#2368; &#2324;&#2352; &#2343;&#2366;&#2352;&#2366; &#2325;&#2375; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2325;&#2370;&#2354; 45 &#2325;&#2367;&#2350;&#2368; &#2325;&#2368; &#2342;&#2370;&#2352;&#2368; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2375; &#2360;&#2350;&#2351; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2340;&#2351; &#2325;&#2352; &#2360;&#2325;&#2340;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;?</p>", "options_en": ["11.5 hours", "12.5 hours", "13.5 hours", "14.5 hours"], "options_hi": ["11.5 &#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2375;", "12.5 &#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2375;", "13.5 &#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2375;", "14.5 &#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2375;"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p>Upstream speed of the boat = 144/24 = 6 km/h</p><p>And, 1008 minutes = 1008/60 = 16.8 hours</p><p>So, downstream speed of the boat = 168/16.8 = 10 km/h</p><p>So, required time = 54/6 + 45/10 = 13.5 hours</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Upstream speed of the boat = 144/24 = 6 km/h</p><p>And, 1008 minutes = 1008/60 = 16.8 hours</p><p>So, downstream speed of the boat = 168/16.8 = 10 km/h</p><p>So, required time = 54/6 + 45/10 = 13.5 hours</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Time, Speed & Distance"}, {"q_en": "<p>A shopkeeper sold an article for Rs. 504 per article, there was a loss of 16%. If the shopkeeper incurs a total loss of Rs. 4128, then how many articles were sold?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2325;&#2367;&#2360;&#2368; &#2342;&#2369;&#2325;&#2366;&#2344;&#2342;&#2366;&#2352; &#2344;&#2375; &#2319;&#2325; &#2357;&#2360;&#2381;&#2340;&#2369; &#2325;&#2379; 504 &#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2351;&#2375; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367; &#2357;&#2360;&#2381;&#2340;&#2369; &#2325;&#2368; &#2342;&#2352; &#2360;&#2375; &#2348;&#2375;&#2330;&#2366;, &#2313;&#2360;&#2375; 16% &#2325;&#2368; &#2361;&#2366;&#2344;&#2367; &#2361;&#2369;&#2312;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2342;&#2369;&#2325;&#2366;&#2344;&#2342;&#2366;&#2352; &#2325;&#2379; &#2325;&#2369;&#2354; 4128 &#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2351;&#2375; &#2325;&#2368; &#2361;&#2366;&#2344;&#2367; &#2361;&#2369;&#2312;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2313;&#2360;&#2344;&#2375; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2368; &#2357;&#2360;&#2381;&#2340;&#2369;&#2319;&#2305; &#2348;&#2375;&#2330;&#2368;&#2306;?</p>", "options_en": ["37", "51", "47", "43"], "options_hi": ["37", "51", "47", "43"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p>S.P = C.P * (100  -  Loss)/100</p><p>504 = C.P * (100  -  16)/100</p><p>C.P = 504 * 100/84 = Rs. 600</p><p>Loss = 600  -  504 = 96</p><p>Hence, the total articles sold = 4128/96 = 43</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>S.P = C.P * (100  -  Loss)/100</p><p>504 = C.P * (100  -  16)/100</p><p>C.P = 504 * 100/84 = Rs. 600</p><p>Loss = 600  -  504 = 96</p><p>Hence, the total articles sold = 4128/96 = 43</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Profit & Loss"}, {"q_en": "<p>The bar graph shows the number of students present in a class on four days. The average number of students present on Monday, Tuesday and Wednesday is:</p><p><img width=306 height=210 id=\"Picture 25\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p27164/image023.png\" ></p>", "q_hi": "&#2348;&#2366;&#2352; &#2327;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2347; &#2330;&#2366;&#2352; &#2342;&#2367;&#2344;&#2379;&#2306; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2319;&#2325; &#2325;&#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2366; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2313;&#2346;&#2360;&#2381;&#2341;&#2367;&#2340; &#2331;&#2366;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2368; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2342;&#2352;&#2381;&#2358;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2360;&#2379;&#2350;&#2357;&#2366;&#2352;, &#2350;&#2306;&#2327;&#2354;&#2357;&#2366;&#2352; &#2324;&#2352; &#2348;&#2369;&#2343;&#2357;&#2366;&#2352; &#2325;&#2379; &#2313;&#2346;&#2360;&#2381;&#2341;&#2367;&#2340; &#2331;&#2366;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2368; &#2324;&#2360;&#2340; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;:</p><p><img width=306 height=210 id=\"Picture 25\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p27164/image023.png\" >", "options_en": ["24", "20", "30", "25"], "options_hi": ["24", "20", "30", "25"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p>Total number of students present on Monday, Tuesday and Wednesday together = 25 + 30 + 20 = 75</p><p>Required average = 75/3 = 25</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Total number of students present on Monday, Tuesday and Wednesday together = 25 + 30 + 20 = 75</p><p>Required average = 75/3 = 25</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Percentage"}, {"q_en": "<p>A die is cast thrice and a coin is tossed thrice. Find the probability that the die will turn a 3 each time and the coin will turn a head every time.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2346;&#2366;&#2360;&#2366; &#2340;&#2368;&#2344; &#2348;&#2366;&#2352; &#2313;&#2331;&#2366;&#2354;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376; &#2324;&#2352; &#2319;&#2325; &#2360;&#2367;&#2325;&#2381;&#2325;&#2366; &#2340;&#2368;&#2344; &#2348;&#2366;&#2352; &#2313;&#2331;&#2366;&#2354;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2311;&#2360; &#2348;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2351;&#2367;&#2325;&#2340;&#2366; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319; &#2325;&#2367; &#2346;&#2366;&#2360;&#2366; &#2361;&#2352; &#2348;&#2366;&#2352; 3 &#2310;&#2319;&#2327;&#2366; &#2324;&#2352; &#2360;&#2367;&#2325;&#2381;&#2325;&#2366; &#2361;&#2352; &#2348;&#2366;&#2352; &#2330;&#2367;&#2340; &#2310;&#2319;&#2327;&#2366;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["1/1728", "1/864", "1/432", "1/1152"], "options_hi": ["1/1728", "1/864", "1/432", "1/1152"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p>The probability of coming 3 every time = 1/6 * 1/6 * 1/6 = 1/216</p><p>The probability of head every time = &frac12; * &frac12; * &frac12; = 1/8 </p><p>Hence, the required probability = 1/216 * 1/8 </p><p>= 1/1728 </p>", "solution_hi": "<p>The probability of coming 3 every time = 1/6 * 1/6 * 1/6 = 1/216</p><p>The probability of head every time = &frac12; * &frac12; * &frac12; = 1/8 </p><p>Hence, the required probability = 1/216 * 1/8 </p><p>= 1/1728 </p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Probability"}, {"q_en": "<p>The length of two pillars are 25 m and X m. The distance between them is 16 m. If two angles of elevation of their respective top from the bottom of the other are complementary to each other, find the value of X. </p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2342;&#2379; &#2326;&#2306;&#2349;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2368; &#2354;&#2306;&#2348;&#2366;&#2312; 25 &#2350;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352; &#2324;&#2352; X &#2350;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2313;&#2344;&#2325;&#2375; &#2348;&#2368;&#2330; &#2325;&#2368; &#2342;&#2370;&#2352;&#2368; 16 &#2350;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2319;&#2325; &#2342;&#2370;&#2360;&#2352;&#2375; &#2325;&#2375; &#2340;&#2354; &#2360;&#2375; &#2313;&#2344;&#2325;&#2375; &#2358;&#2368;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359; &#2325;&#2375; &#2313;&#2344;&#2381;&#2344;&#2351;&#2344; &#2325;&#2379;&#2339; &#2319;&#2325; &#2342;&#2370;&#2360;&#2352;&#2375; &#2325;&#2375; &#2346;&#2370;&#2352;&#2325; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;, &#2340;&#2379; X &#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["10.24 m", "12 m", "14.5 m", "9.8 m"], "options_hi": ["10.24 &#2350;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352;", "12 &#2350;&#2368;", "14.5 &#2350;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352;", "9.8 &#2350;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352;"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p><img width=259 height=165 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p27673/image007.png\" ></p><p>We know that when A + B = 90 then distance between = &radic;(Product of height of pillars)</p><p>16 = &radic;(25 x X)</p><p>X = 256/25 = 10.24 m</p>", "solution_hi": "<p><img width=259 height=165 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p27673/image007.png\" ></p><p>We know that when A + B = 90 then distance between = &radic;(Product of height of pillars)</p><p>16 = &radic;(25 x X)</p><p>X = 256/25 = 10.24 m</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Height & Distance"}, {"q_en": "<p>For a sample data, mean = 60 and median = 48. For this distribution, the mode is:</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2344;&#2350;&#2370;&#2344;&#2375; &#2325;&#2375; &#2310;&#2305;&#2325;&#2396;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2375; &#2354;&#2367;&#2319; &#2350;&#2366;&#2343;&#2381;&#2351; = 60 &#2324;&#2352; &#2350;&#2366;&#2343;&#2381;&#2351;&#2367;&#2325;&#2366; = 48 &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2311;&#2360; &#2357;&#2367;&#2340;&#2352;&#2339; &#2325;&#2375; &#2354;&#2367;&#2319;, &#2348;&#2361;&#2369;&#2354;&#2325; &#2361;&#2376;:</p>", "options_en": ["18", "48", "36", "24"], "options_hi": ["18", "48", "36", "24"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p>Mode = 3*median  -  2*mean</p><p>= 3*48  -  2*60</p><p>= 144  -  120</p><p>= 24</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Mode = 3*median  -  2*mean</p><p>= 3*48  -  2*60</p><p>= 144  -  120</p><p>= 24</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Statistics"}, {"q_en": "<p>If x = 11, then the value of (x<sup>5</sup> - 12x<sup>4</sup> + 12x<sup>3</sup> - 12x<sup>2</sup> + 12x - 1) is:</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; x = 11 &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; (x<sup>5</sup> - 12x<sup>4</sup> + 12x<sup>3</sup> - 12x<sup>2</sup> + 12x - 1) &#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2361;&#2376;:</p>", "options_en": ["10", "8", "9", "14"], "options_hi": ["10", "8", "9", "14"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p>x = 11 </p><p>x<sup>5</sup> - 12x<sup>4</sup> + 12x<sup>3</sup> - 12x<sup>2</sup> + 12x  -  1</p><p>= 11<sup>5</sup>  -  12 * 11<sup>4</sup> + 12 * 11<sup>3</sup>  -  12 * 11<sup>2</sup> + 12 * 11  -  1</p><p>= 11<sup>5</sup>  -  11 * 11<sup>4</sup>  -  11<sup>4</sup> + 11 * 11<sup>3</sup> + 11<sup>3</sup>  -  11 * 11<sup>2</sup>  -  11<sup>2</sup> + 11 * 11 + 11 - 1</p><p>= 11<sup>5</sup>  -  11<sup>5</sup>  -  11<sup>4</sup> + 11<sup>4</sup> + 11<sup>3</sup>  -  11<sup>3</sup>  -  11<sup>2</sup> + 11<sup>2</sup> + 11 - 1</p><p>= 11  -  1</p><p>= 10</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>x = 11 </p><p>x<sup>5</sup> - 12x<sup>4</sup> + 12x<sup>3</sup> - 12x<sup>2</sup> + 12x  -  1</p><p>= 11<sup>5</sup>  -  12 * 11<sup>4</sup> + 12 * 11<sup>3</sup>  -  12 * 11<sup>2</sup> + 12 * 11  -  1</p><p>= 11<sup>5</sup>  -  11 * 11<sup>4</sup>  -  11<sup>4</sup> + 11 * 11<sup>3</sup> + 11<sup>3</sup>  -  11 * 11<sup>2</sup>  -  11<sup>2</sup> + 11 * 11 + 11 - 1</p><p>= 11<sup>5</sup>  -  11<sup>5</sup>  -  11<sup>4</sup> + 11<sup>4</sup> + 11<sup>3</sup>  -  11<sup>3</sup>  -  11<sup>2</sup> + 11<sup>2</sup> + 11 - 1</p><p>= 11  -  1</p><p>= 10</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Algebra"}]}